# Every seeded example on a surface in this repo — the grey text in an empty
# field, and any element marked `data-example` — and where it came from. Held by
# the hub's `example-check.mjs`, which says why this is a declared list rather
# than a rule about content: an invented scenario and a real one are the same
# sentence, so the only checkable fact is whether anybody ever stated which.
#
# An example taken from somebody's actual work is not declarable and never
# becomes declarable. Invent the scenario.
#
# Everything below is a HINT ABOUT THE FIELD rather than a sample value, which is
# this app's habit and worth keeping: a spool placeholder reading "eSUN PLA+
# Cold White" would be somebody's shelf, and a model placeholder would be
# somebody's print. None of these name a filament, a printer, a maker or a
# model, and none of them can be traced to a real object.
#
#   file | invented | product-copy | public-data | the example's opening words

public/index.html | invented | Paste the address they sent
public/index.html | invented | What is being printed
public/index.html | invented | Whatever you call it
public/index.html | invented | Paste the address of the model
public/index.html | invented | Separated by commas
